# Starter community Q&As (20 Nov 2026). Answered by "Legal Wegal Expert". (category, question, answer)
QA = [
("GST", "Is GST registration required if my turnover is below ₹20 lakh?",
 "Not always. Service businesses need it above ₹20 lakh turnover and goods businesses above ₹40 lakh (lower limits in special category states). But it is compulsory regardless of turnover if you sell goods interstate, sell on e-commerce marketplaces, or fall in other notified categories. Many small businesses register voluntarily so they can issue GST invoices to bigger clients."),
("GST", "I registered for GST but had no sales. Do I still need to file returns?",
 "Yes. Every registered person must file GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B for every period, even with zero sales (a nil return). Late fees apply for missed nil returns too, and continued non-filing can lead to cancellation of your GSTIN."),
("GST", "Can I cancel my GST registration if I closed my business?",
 "Yes. You can apply for cancellation on the GST portal (Form REG-16). Before that, file all pending returns and pay any dues. After cancellation you must also file a final return (GSTR-10) within three months."),
("GST", "What is the QRMP scheme in GST?",
 "QRMP (Quarterly Return Monthly Payment) lets businesses with turnover up to ₹5 crore file GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B quarterly while paying tax monthly. It reduces the number of returns but you still pay tax every month."),
("Company", "Can one person register a Private Limited Company?",
 "A Private Limited Company needs at least two directors and two shareholders. A single founder can register a One Person Company (OPC) instead, and convert it into a Private Limited Company later."),
("Company", "Is there a minimum capital needed to start a Private Limited Company?",
 "No. There is no minimum paid-up capital requirement now. You can start with any amount, for example ₹10,000 or ₹1 lakh, depending on your needs. Stamp duty depends on the authorised capital and your state."),
("Company", "Which is better for a small consultancy: LLP or Private Limited?",
 "If you do not plan to raise equity funding, an LLP is usually cheaper to run because the audit is needed only above certain limits and annual filings are simpler. If you want investors or ESOPs, choose a Private Limited Company."),
("Company", "Can a salaried employee become a director of a company?",
 "Generally yes, as long as your employment contract does not prohibit it and you disclose it to your employer where required. Check your appointment letter and company policy before you start."),
("Trademark", "Can I use ® after filing my trademark application?",
 "No. The ® symbol can be used only after the trademark is registered. After filing you can use the ™ symbol to show that you claim the mark."),
("Trademark", "My trademark application got an objection. What should I do?",
 "File a reply (examination report response) within the time given, usually 30 days. The reply should address each ground of objection with arguments and evidence of use. Many objections are cleared with a well-drafted reply or at a hearing."),
("Trademark", "How long is a trademark valid in India?",
 "A registered trademark is valid for 10 years from the date of application and can be renewed every 10 years indefinitely by paying the renewal fee."),
("FSSAI", "Do home bakers need an FSSAI registration?",
 "Yes. Anyone selling food, including home bakers and tiffin services, needs at least a basic FSSAI registration if turnover is up to ₹12 lakh a year. Above that, a state licence is needed."),
("FSSAI", "Can I sell on Swiggy or Zomato without FSSAI?",
 "No. Food delivery platforms require a valid FSSAI registration or licence number before they list your kitchen or restaurant."),
("Licences", "Is hallmarking compulsory for all gold jewellery?",
 "Hallmarking with HUID is mandatory for gold jewellery and artefacts sold in notified districts, which cover most of India. Jewellers there must register with BIS and sell only hallmarked items. A few categories and small weights are exempt."),
("Licences", "Do I need an IEC to export services?",
 "IEC is mainly needed to import or export goods. For services, it is needed if you want to claim export benefits under the Foreign Trade Policy. Getting one is quick and the DGFT fee is ₹500."),
("Licences", "Is Udyam registration free?",
 "Yes, the government charges no fee for Udyam registration. Service providers charge only for the help with filing. It is entirely online and based on Aadhaar, PAN and GST details."),
("Tax", "What is the last date to file an income tax return?",
 "For individuals and businesses not requiring an audit, the due date is usually 31 July after the financial year. Audit cases have later dates. You can still file a belated return later, but a late fee and interest may apply."),
("Tax", "Do I need to file an ITR if my income is below the taxable limit?",
 "It is not compulsory in every case, but filing is recommended. It helps with loans, visas and claiming refunds of TDS. It is compulsory in certain cases, such as high foreign travel spends, large electricity bills or high bank deposits."),
("Legal", "Is a rent agreement on stamp paper necessary?",
 "A rent agreement should be on stamp paper of the value prescribed by your state. Agreements of 12 months or more must also be registered. Many states have e-stamping and online registration, which makes it simple."),
("Legal", "How soon must I send a notice if a cheque bounces?",
 "Under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, the legal notice must be sent within 30 days of receiving the bank's return memo. The drawer then has 15 days to pay; if they don't, you can file a complaint within the next month."),
]
